  "notes": "{捕|つか}まる has two main meanings: 'to be caught/arrested' and 'to hold onto something.'\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive)\n- Pair: {捕|つか}まえる (transitive, to catch)\n\nSENSE 1 - Be caught:\n- {犯人|はんにん}が{捕|つか}まる: a criminal is caught\n- {警察|けいさつ}に{捕|つか}まる: to be caught by police\n- タクシーが{捕|つか}まらない: can't catch a taxi\n\nSENSE 2 - Hold onto:\n- {手|て}すりに{捕|つか}まる: to hold onto the handrail\n- {吊|つ}り{革|かわ}に{捕|つか}まる: to hold onto the strap (on train)\n\nKANJI NOTE:\n{捕|つか}まる uses {捕|ほ} (capture). The related verb {掴|つか}む (to grab) uses different kanji.",
